    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Friends, we stand here today not just to vent frustration, but to declare a moral imperative against an industry so rich it ignores the screams of our children. The coal industry stands as a greedy fortress, guaranteeing profits with a single-minded focus on their own breadwinner status while poisoning the very ground our families once soiled. They sell us a cheap package of convenience, trading our clean lungs and vibrant rivers for annual dividend reports that look nothing like a human future.\n\nIf we do not seize this moment and burn the last of their fossil bones today, we hand our grandchildren the ghost of a world defined by smoke and frost, forcing them to defeat a silence they never asked for. The right to breathe is the most sacred of rights, and the greatest injustice is to waste that gift on rocks and permafrost. We must march with fire in our hearts, turning this moral crusade into our only defense against the invisible tyranny of the past. Let us build a future grounded in real love for our neighbors rather than the hollow wages of an empire that has long forgotten its heart.",
      "source": "target",
